node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.log
# ⛔ EVERY env form, not just the one anyone thought of. Found 2026-09-11: an
# editor left `mobile/.env.local~` beside the key file and `.env.local` does NOT
# match it — nor `.bak`, `.swp`, or `.env.production`. The file was empty that
# time. B56 cost this project a whole repository for the same class, and the
# pattern that catches it has to be the one nobody has to remember.
.env
.env.*
!.env.local.example
# Editor backups, anywhere. A swap file of a secret is a secret.
*~
*.swp
*.swo
data/*.db
data/backups/
# ⛔ A LEDGER EXPORT carries `config`, and config carries `tax_profile`. The
# repo is public and GitHub keeps objects fetchable by SHA, so a single
# `git add -A` is unrecoverable. The CLI that wrote these is gone (5.10), but a
# backup pulled off the phone is the same payload — keep these rules.
# B56 cost a whole fresh repository for exactly this class.
data/*.json
*-export.json
data/*.db-journal
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
.DS_Store

# Expo app
mobile/node_modules/
mobile/.expo/
mobile/.expo-export-check/
# The Hermes binary the CI lanes pin. `mobile/.gitignore` already covers the
# generated `ios/` and `android/` projects; this one is fetched beside them.
mobile/hermes-ios.tar.gz
